executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Worktree-mode resume. When the registered W on moe/task/<id> has no per-worktree index file, the wrapper finishes W (sparse-checkout set, then read-tree -mu HEAD) only if W's directory holds exactly one entry, .git.

Otherwise it refuses with MOE_WORKTREE_CREATE_FAILED '<W> has no index file but holds more than .git; a human must inspect it':
- one [ERROR] line;
- exactly one report_blocked;
- no CLI;
- exit 1;
- W's files, and its missing index, are left untouched.

The rule and the message are the same in moe-agent.sh (provision_worktree) and moe-agent.ps1 (Install-MoeTaskWorktree).
